35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The timing data shows a full pass takes over an hour and a half. Meanwhile, a professional firm requires us to tidy up first, meaning we wouldn't be entirely free from the labor.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really interesting stuff! It turns out some of us are away way more than others, and only a few people are actually making the kitchen messy. That's a huge difference!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings confirm that our standards for ""done"" vary significantly, which creates inconsistency. Furthermore, our past arguments in the chat always began with reminders about unfinished tasks. It seems our friction stems from these mismatched expectations.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out we're spending about 2,300 yen a month on spray, but we're buying things twice! Also, the management office cleaner is 4,200 yen an hour. We really need a better way to track our money!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that the bathroom grout gets dirty again in just eleven days because of the ventilation. Also, the previous tenants' note said they split the rooms permanently, but they ended up barely speaking.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, if usage is uneven, a flat rotation is illogical. However, @Victoria's point about standards means that even if we hire someone, we still spend time managing the ""tidying"" and the quality. We need a solution that minimizes total time.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! If some of us are barely here or just making coffee, it doesn't feel right to do the same amount of scrubbing as the people cooking big meals every day. We should definitely consider that!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, while usage patterns matter, we must be careful. If we base duties solely on usage, it might lead to resentment or constant monitoring of each other. We need a system that feels fair without becoming a source of surveillance.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, @Victoria, we can't just think about time! We're wasting money buying the same things twice! Whoever is paying for the spray is probably getting tired of it. We need a money pot or a better list!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about the bathroom. If it gets dirty in only eleven days, no matter who cleans it, it'll always feel... grim. And the note from the previous tenants makes me scared that we'll stop talking to each other.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the grout issue suggests we need a higher frequency of cleaning, not just a different person. @Rin, a shared fund is a simple fix, but it doesn't solve the labor problem. We must prioritize the time commitment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, I agree that frequency is key, but we can't just add more work for everyone! If we balance the chores based on who's actually using the rooms, it won't feel like such a burden.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I understand your point, but monitoring usage can be invasive. @Daisuke, the previous tenants' experience is a warning. We should prioritize a system that prevents resentment, even if it means a slightly less ""efficient"" distribution of labor.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,But we can't have harmony if someone is secretly broke because they bought all the sponges! A shared fund isn't just about money; it's about being kind to each other's wallets! Let's fix the money and the cleaning together!,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just don't want us to fight. If we can find a way to keep the bathroom clean more often without making anyone feel burdened, maybe we can avoid what happened to the previous tenants.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We have a conflict between efficiency, fairness, and harmony. Since the total labor is significant and the grout degrades quickly, we need a system that is predictable and doesn't rely on constant monitoring or negotiation.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I get that, but predictability shouldn't mean ignoring the facts! If we just stick to a rigid plan, the people who are always here and cooking will still feel like they're doing all the heavy lifting. We can be fair and predictable!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I believe the most dangerous path is one that requires us to constantly police each other's habits. Let's choose a system that minimizes the need for reminders, as those are what trigger our conflicts.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I agree! Let's make a system where we don't have to nag each other. But please, can we also agree on a shared money pot for supplies? It'll be like a little treasure chest for the house!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think I agree. If we have a clear plan and a shared fund, maybe we won't have to argue. I just want to feel safe and calm when I'm at home.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
