60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is inefficient because we still have to tidy up first, and the cost is high. Option A risks the resentment the previous tenants faced. Option B is the most logical for distributing the labor burden.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I don't know about Option B! If we just rotate, the people who are always here and making the mess still get a ""free pass"" when it's not their week. That doesn't feel fair at all!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I understand your concern, but Option B removes the need for constant reminders. If we have a fixed rota, the responsibility is clear, which prevents the kind of nagging that leads to arguments.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I like Option C! If a pro does it, we won't fight about how clean it is. Plus, we can just add the cleaning cost to our shared money pot! It's the easiest way!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm worried about Option A because of that note. But Option B might be okay if we all agree on the standards... I just want to know it'll be clean. Maybe Option C is safest?,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Rin, @Daisuke, Option C is a financial drain and doesn't eliminate the labor of tidying. @Mio, while a rota isn't perfect, it's the only way to ensure the total time burden is shared equally without constant surveillance.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Daisuke"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"But it's not equal if the usage isn't equal! If I'm the only one cooking for a week, I'm still cleaning up after myself, but I'm also doing the ""rota"" work. It just feels wrong!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, if we try to adjust for every single meal or visit, we will spend more time arguing over the math than actually cleaning. A rota is a social contract that lets us move past the ""who did what"" phase.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"But if we do Option B, we still have to figure out who pays for the soap! If we pick Option C, the money part is already solved because we just split the bill! It's way simpler!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Victoria is right about the arguing. If we spend all our time calculating who used the kitchen more, we might end up like the previous tenants. I'll vote for Option B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Rin, the money pot is a separate issue from the labor system; we can implement it regardless of the option. Option B is the only one that guarantees a predictable, shared time commitment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I guess you're right about the arguing, but I still hate the idea of it being unfair! If we go with Option B, can we at least promise to be extra helpful when someone is away?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"That is a kind gesture, Mio, and I think that spirit of flexibility is exactly what will keep us on speaking terms. As long as the framework is clear, we can support each other without it feeling like a chore.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"If we can have the money pot for the soap and sponges no matter what, then Option B sounds okay! It's like a team game where we take turns! I'll vote for B!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I feel a bit better now that we're agreeing. If we all help each other and use the money pot, maybe it'll be okay. I'll vote for Option B too.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Since we have reached a consensus that Option B provides the most predictable distribution of labor and minimizes conflict, I will also vote for Option B. It is the most rational choice for the household.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm still a little worried about the fairness, but I don't want us to fight! If we all promise to be kind and help out, I'm in. I'll vote for Option B too!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. A clear, rotating structure protects our relationships by removing ambiguity. I vote for Option B, and I look forward to us maintaining this harmony throughout the year.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"Yay! We're all on the same team now! As long as we get that treasure chest for the cleaning supplies so nobody's wallet gets sad, I'm super happy! I vote for Option B!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we could decide together. I feel much more relieved knowing there's a plan we all agree on. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
